// Mercury-Atlas (LV-3B) (1962).
// Atlas is a stage and a half: the sustainer's balloon tank holds all the propellant, and
// its LR105 burns from liftoff through the booster skirt, whose two LR89s draw on that
// tank across a crossfeed decoupler until the skirt drops at two minutes. Built from
// plain parts.
